course: dictionary
lesson: 11622
title: Approximately: about, not exactly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Approximately means close to an exact amount, number or time, but not exactly. It means about. «There are approximately 30 children in our class» means the number is close to 30, perhaps 28 or 31, but nobody has counted them exactly.
explain: Use approximately when a number is close enough. «The bus arrives at approximately half past nine» means it comes around that time, not on the dot.
explain: In maths, the sign ≈ means "is approximately equal to". You can estimate, or round a number, and then say the answer is approximately right. Approximately tells the reader it is close, but not exact.
fact: Approximately is an adverb, because it tells you how close something is.
fact: «Approximately» means close to, but not exactly; about.
fact: The sign ≈ means "is approximately equal to", so 19 ≈ 20.
fact: Useful phrases are "approximately equal" and "approximately how many".
fact: In science, measurements are often approximate, because it is hard to measure something exactly.
exercise: «The jar holds approximately one litre of water.» What does approximately mean here? | Ten litres | Exactly one litre | Completely empty | *About one litre, but not exactly
exercise: Which sign means "is approximately equal to"? | *≈ | < | > | =
exercise: 28 is close to 30, so 28 is approximately which number? | 20 | 40 | *30 | 25
test: «The walk to school takes approximately twenty minutes.» What does approximately tell us? | It takes an hour | It takes exactly twenty minutes | *It takes about twenty minutes, give or take | It never takes twenty minutes
test: Which sentence uses approximately correctly? | I have approximately 3 apples, and I have counted every one | *The park is approximately two kilometres away | My birthday is approximately today, to the second | There are approximately 30 children, and I counted exactly 30
exam: Mia says 19 ≈ 20. What does the sign mean? | 19 is exactly 20 | 19 and 20 are the same word | *19 is approximately equal to 20, close but not exact | 19 is much bigger than 20
